                                li
                                    a(href="https://rstudio.github.io/cheatsheets/html/data-visualization.html") ggplot2
                li Practice
                    ul
                        li Get access to a terminal on your lap/desk-top.
                            br
                            a(href="Lecture/W1Day1/ServerAccess.pdf") Instructions on how to access the terminal to practice.
                        li An introduction to the <b>unix/linux command line</b>. Do the 10 steps listed on:
                            br
                            a(href="http://linuxcommand.org/lc3_learning_the_shell.php") LinuxCommand.org.
                        li An introduction to the <b>R language and environment</b>
                            a(href="materials/Torfs+Brauer-Short-R-Intro.pdf") - Install RStudio on your computer (if you have not already) and go through the doc (about 2h)
                        li For a more in depth introduction to R, check the book from Hadley Wickham: 
                            a(href="https://r4ds.hadley.nz") R for Data Science
                            p Read and do chapter 1-3 (minimum requirement for the course); chapter 4-8 (mimimum requirement for your own data analysis); all (if you aim at professional data science)
            ul
                li Read
